@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Authoritative Share Manifest
  "Models, validates, serializes, and indexes the remote manifest.json schema (v1)."

  Provides:
    - domain.ManifestVersion @source("symbol:ManifestVersion")
    - domain.EndpointState @source("symbol:EndpointState")
    - domain.Manifest @source("symbol:Manifest")
    - domain.Blob @source("symbol:Blob")
    - domain.Share @source("symbol:Share")
    - domain.Endpoint @source("symbol:Endpoint")
    - domain.SlugEndpoint @source("symbol:SlugEndpoint")
    - domain.Indexes @source("symbol:Indexes")
    - domain.NewManifest @source("symbol:NewManifest")
    - domain.ParseManifest @source("symbol:ParseManifest")
    - domain.MarshalManifest @source("symbol:MarshalManifest")
    - domain.Manifest.Validate @source("symbol:Validate")
    - domain.EndpointState.Valid @source("symbol:Valid")
    - domain.Share.EndpointRefCount @source("symbol:EndpointRefCount")
    - domain.Share.Active @source("symbol:Active")
    - domain.Manifest.BlobRefCount @source("symbol:BlobRefCount")
    - domain.Manifest.BlobRefCounts @source("symbol:BlobRefCounts")
    - domain.Manifest.OrphanedBlobs @source("symbol:OrphanedBlobs")
    - domain.BuildIndexes @source("symbol:BuildIndexes")
    - domain.Manifest.FindShareByPath @source("symbol:FindShareByPath")
    - domain.Manifest.FindShareBySlug @source("symbol:FindShareBySlug")

  Consumes:
    - domain.BlobHex
    - domain.NormalizeObjectPath
    - domain.ValidateSlug

  Invariants:
    - Manifest version MUST be ManifestVersion (1)
    - Each share MUST retain at least one endpoint (path and/or slug)
    - Object paths and slug identities MUST be unique across active shares
    - Every slug endpoint value MUST appear in reserved_slugs
    - Blob reference counts MUST count manifest endpoints; disabled endpoints still count
    - OrphanedBlobs MUST list blobs with zero endpoint references

  Scenario (happy-path): Parse valid manifest
    Given well-formed manifest JSON at version 1
    When ParseManifest runs
    Then a validated Manifest is returned

  Scenario (happy-path): Orphan detection
    Given blobs listed with no share endpoints referencing them
    When OrphanedBlobs runs
    Then those blob keys are returned sorted

  Scenario (negative): Duplicate object path
    Given two shares claiming the same object path
    When Validate runs
    Then it returns a duplicate path error

  Scenario (negative): Unreserved slug
    Given a share slug not present in reserved_slugs
    When Validate runs
    Then it returns an error
